==Russian==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|ru|по́ломя}}

===Etymology===
{{root|ru|ine-pro|*pelh₁-}}
Via {{inh|ru|zle-mru|-}}, then probably borrowed {{der|ru|zle-ops|*полꙑмѧ}}, from {{der|ru|sla-pro|*pòlmy}}{{dercat|ru|ine-bsl-pro|ine-pro}}. Cognate with {{cog|be|по́лымя}}.

{{doublet|ru|пла́мя|по́ломя}}, where the first one is an Old Church Slavonic word showing [[w:liquid metathesis|liquid metathesis]] characteristic of South Slavic area, and the second one normally inherited by [[w:pleophony|pleophony]] of *TorT > *ToroT type, while {{cog|zle-ops|-}} dialect ([[w:Krivichs|Krivichs]] area) reflex of [[w:Pleophony|pleophony]] {{m|und||*TolT}} > {{m|und||*TolᵊT}}, {{m|und||*TolᵒT}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA|по́лымя|ann=y}}
* {{ru-IPA|полымя́|ann=y}}

===Noun===
{{ru-noun|по́лымя,полымя́|n-in|manual=1}}

# {{lb|ru|obsolete|or|poetic}} {{synonym of|ru|пла́мя}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[из огня́ да в по́лымя]]|[[out of the frying pan into the fire]]}}

